<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh to receive $210 million U.S. aid.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh to receive $210 million U.S. aid.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh will receive $210 million in aid from the United States to finance a population control education project, finance ministry officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>The project aims to bring down the country's annual population growth rate from the present 1.8 percent by teaching families about contraception and other aspects of family planning and health care.</p>
<p>Impoverished Bangladesh has 122 million people with an annual per capita income of just $240.</p>
</text>
